The overall clarity and quality is good, but I have the following concerns:


1. It is unreasonable to use the learned representation of the method-level snippet for the main method in the class declaration as the class-level representation. What if the class has other methods invoked by the main method?  For example: 
```
public class MyClass {

  public static void foo(String[] args) {
    doSomething();
  }
  public static void main(String[] args) {
    ...
    foo(args);
    ...
  }
}
```


Minors:


1. How many problems are chosen from codeforce?

2. Section 3.3 is more like an engineering effort, so putting it in section 4 might be a better choice.

3. I would prefer that Figure 1 is introduced right after "Then, we aggregate the information of the entire code by processing the embeddings computed from each code snippet by the higher-level Transformer.". Because the paragraph where Figure 1 is introduced mainly discusses "multi-level pre-training objectives".

4. Figure 4 should be redesigned for a better layout.

5. Table 3 is referred before Table 2.

6. I am a bit confused about why authors evaluate many baselines but do not have an in-depth evaluation of the proposed method. In other words, I would expect to see the performance of the proposed method integrated with other models, e.g., GraphCodeBERT+HA, PLBART+HA.

